[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:16-19[39m:

  - A native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m so the text is clickable — the input itself holds the on/off
    state, no JS needed.
  - One CSS rule strikes through and dims the label when checked, so "done" is visible.

  No tests or build in this repo, so nothing to run. If you want multiple task items, or the checked state to survive a
  reload (localStorage), say the word — that's where JS starts being worth it.

